From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:23:43 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: apple: macaudio: Take each SN012776's amp level from
 the DT

The driver limited every SN012776's "Amp Gain Volume" to a value from
its per-board table; three of those values (J614s, J616s, J713) were
picked at bring-up. The Mac's ADT gives each amp's operating level: the
second byte of the amp's row in its group's speaker-config, which the
boot loader now copies to the amp's node as apple,speaker-config.

Limit each SN012776's "Amp Gain Volume" to its own level from that row
(low five bits) and drop the SN012776 gains from the board tables. A
speaker link whose amps do not all carry a level in the amp's range
(an older boot loader) keeps its speakers off, as a model whose safety
the driver can't assure does. The woofers keep the playback high-pass
corner the amps were given from the ADT (apple,amp-dcblocker-config)
instead of a fixed "2 Hz"; the tweeters keep the 800 Hz protection
floor.

On the M1 Pro, M2 and M4 Pro every amp's ADT level is the level their
tables had, so their limits do not change.

KUnit apple-speaker-amp-level (4 cases): the level is the row's second
byte, out-of-range and short or absent rows are rejected, speakers need
every amp's level, no SN012776 board table carries a gain.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit 44f56e6b03d19af8efc2c4a6ea1d2b88d82eb307)

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
